course: dictionary
lesson: 14364
title: Opposable thumbs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Try touching the tip of your thumb to the tip of each finger. Your thumb can swing round to face your fingers, and that is what makes it opposable. Opposable means able to be placed opposite and pressed against the other fingers, so the hand can grip and pick things up.
explain: Break the word into two parts. Oppose means to set against or face, and -able means can be done. So an opposable thumb can be turned to face the fingers. Check it in a sentence: «Our opposable thumbs help us pick up a pencil.» Swap in the meaning: thumbs that can face the fingers help us pick up a pencil. That makes sense.
explain: Scientists use this word when they study humans, apes and monkeys. «Chimpanzees use their opposable thumbs to hold sticks.» A stick is hard to hold with only fingers that all point the same way, but a thumb that can meet the fingers gives a strong grip.
fact: Opposable means able to be placed opposite and pressed against the other fingers, like a human thumb.
fact: «Opposable thumbs» let humans, apes and many monkeys hold tools, write and climb.
fact: Some animals, like koalas and opossums, have opposable digits on their feet or hands.
fact: Oppose means to set against or face, and -able means can be done.
fact: A thumb that can meet the fingers makes it easier to pick up small things, like a pin or a pea.
exercise: «Our opposable thumbs help us pick up a pencil.» What does opposable mean here? | *Able to press against the other fingers | Coloured bright blue | Able to fly through the air | Very long and thin
exercise: «The koala used its opposable digits to grip the branch.» What do the opposable digits help the koala do? | Sing loudly at night | *Hold on to a branch | Swim fast in a river | Read a book
exercise: Which word means able to be placed opposite and pressed against the other fingers? | *Opposable | Sticky | Hollow | Fragile
test: Which animal has opposable digits on its feet? | Horse | Dolphin | *Opossum | Cow
test: Why are opposable thumbs useful for holding tools? | *Because they can press against the other fingers and grip | Because they glow in the dark | Because they are very long | Because they can swim
exam: «Koalas and humans both have opposable digits.» Why is an opposable digit useful to a koala? | It lets the koala glow | It makes the koala lighter | It stops the koala from sleeping | *It can wrap around a branch and grip tightly
